Subject: web: pass the startup check when any bundled agent is ready

Why: the web shim's checkEnvironment requires Claude Code and Codex, so a
Host release that bundles only Pi (the fnOS app) never leaves the
"环境初始化失败" startup screen and the original login UI is unreachable.
Upstream: not yet proposed (issue draft to follow; related to the merged
https://github.com/makecindy/cindy/pull/10418).
Remove when: upstream's web startup check accepts a release without Claude
Code and Codex.

diff --git a/apps/web/shim.js b/apps/web/shim.js
index f064ed0e69..0ca2a94fbb 100644
--- a/apps/web/shim.js
+++ b/apps/web/shim.js
@@ -512,7 +512,8 @@ import { startHostEventStream } from '@cindy/maker-shared/host-event-stream';
     'checkEnvironment': () => {
       const harness = window.__cindyBoot?.harness ?? {};
       const entry = (ready) => (ready ? { status: 'passed' } : { status: 'failed', error: 'not installed' });
-      const allPassed = Boolean(harness['claude-code'] && harness.codex);
+      // A Host release may bundle only some agents (build --harnesses); any ready one is enough.
+      const allPassed = Boolean(harness['claude-code'] || harness.codex || harness.pi);
       return {
         claudeCode: entry(harness['claude-code']),
         codex: entry(harness.codex),
